title: Received Ye the Spirit by Works?
description: Posts from the channel on Galatians 3 and 5: the "repent of your sins" gospel is the Galatian error of being made perfect by the flesh; we are saved by believing on the Son.
output: lessons/posts/pulled-received-ye-the-spirit-by-works.html

# From the posts of 2023-08-03 (two) and 2024-08-18
# (studies/data/notes/pulled-received-ye-the-spirit-by-works.html), in the author's words.

=== Introduction
--- Received Ye the Spirit by Works? [title]
overline: From the channel
heading: Received Ye the Spirit by Works?
sub: "Repent of your sins" and the Galatian error.
refs: Galatians 3:2; Galatians 5:4; John 3:36
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== How are we saved?
--- Never once quoted scripture
lead: I just listened to a 4-minute audio clip titled "How do you actually get saved according to the Word of God?" that never once quoted scripture, used unbiblical terms like "repent of your sins," "admit you're desperately wicked," "make Jesus your boss," "make Jesus your Lord," that finished with strawman and ad hominem in defense of this damnable heresy.
callout: No one can get saved by someone telling them this.

--- Saved by this truth
p: They are saved by this truth;
big: John 3:36 | mark: He that believeth on the Son hath everlasting life

--- He did it all
- It is not how bad we feel about being a sinner.
- It isn't how well we do walking in the Spirit.
- It isn't how willing we are to enter into discipleship.
lead: It is believing in your heart that Jesus Christ is the Son of God, as the eunuch professed, period.
big: Acts 8:37 | mark: I believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God
center: **He did it all.**

=== The foolish Galatians
--- Led astray by Judaizers
lead: The foolish Galatians had been being led astray by Judaizers who snuck in to spy out their liberty, and to falsely teach that they were not saved unless they did certain things, and made an outward change that was visible to men. [[Galatians 2:4]]
p: Starting with circumcision but adding other Judaized concepts to the faith, and making it to none effect.

--- Made perfect by the flesh?
scripture: Galatians 3:1-3 | mark: Received ye the Spirit by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith; having begun in the Spirit, are ye now made perfect by the flesh

--- Exactly the same thing
lead: "Repent-of-your-sins" heresy is exactly the same thing.
p: That while you *may* begin in the Spirit, you are made perfect in the flesh. That a change must come, and outward signs observable to these hypocritical fruit inspectors, or else you must doubt your salvation. You must be made complete by the flesh to satisfy their own judgment.
callout: It is as wicked now as it was then.

--- Christ shall profit you nothing
lead: Behold, I Jag say unto you, that if you are trusting your own turning from sins, Christ shall profit you nothing.
p: Just as Paul warned the Galatians about circumcision. It is the same spirit of placing your trust in things you do rather than Christ. [[Galatians 5:2]]
scripture: Galatians 5:3-4 | mark: ye are fallen from grace
quote: For I testify again to every man that [TRUSTING IN SOMETHING THEY DO], that he is a debtor to do the whole law. | Galatians 5:3, applied

=== The objections
--- "This is different!"
quote: No! Circumcision was part of the law, this is different! I am saying you have to stop sinning! | The objection
big: 1 John 3:4 | mark: sin is the transgression of the law

--- "But James 2!"
quote: But...but...James 2! | The objection
p: Yes. Let us look at James 2:8-13.
scripture: James 2:8-13 | mark: ye have respect to persons; he shall have judgment without mercy, that hath shewed no mercy

--- To whom?
quote: But the fruit of the Spirit should be OBVIOUS! | The objection
lead: To whom? To you? Who the Hell are you, respecter of persons?
- You who show no mercy on judgment?
- You who think the work begun in the Spirit now must be finished in the flesh?
- You who have fallen from grace?
p: Who are you to demand evidence observable to you, and your standards, of another who has believed unto righteousness the gospel of God?

--- Hypocrite! [title]
heading: Hypocrite!
scripture: Matthew 23:4-5 | mark: all their works they do for to be seen of men
big: Matthew 23:13 | mark: ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men

=== Scripture, not men
--- About men
p: And here's the thing. These unsaved fools who are pushing this nonsense want to make it an argument about individuals. About men. Because they feel they can win an argument about men and convince people that because so and so did something, real or slanderously reported, then the doctrine of the Gospel is no good.
callout: They don't make it about scripture because they can't win that argument.

--- Not of ourselves
lead: I've just shown conclusively from scripture again and again and again how we are saved and it is by believing on the Lord Jesus Christ, through the grace of God unto eternal life.
p: Not of ourselves. It is a gift.
big: Ephesians 2:8-9
p: And I can confidently go throughout the Bible and show exactly that salvation is not of us but of Christ.

--- Ignore them [title]
heading: Ignore them
p: Anyone who wants to make the argument about something other than the actual scriptures is a false teacher and they should be ignored.
